.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt EXFAT 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm exfat
.Nd "Extended File Allocation Table file system"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To link into the kernel:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "options EXFAT"
.Ed
.Pp
To load as a loadable kernel module:
.Pp
.Dl "kldload exfat"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver permits the
.Fx
kernel to read and write exFAT (Extended File Allocation Table) file systems.
.Pp
The exFAT file system is commonly used on high-capacity flash storage media,
such as SDXC cards and USB flash drives, where the 4 GiB maximum file size
and 2 TiB volume size limitations of FAT32 are restrictive.
.Pp
Features supported by the
.Nm
driver include:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Full read and write capabilities.
.It
Support for file and volume sizes up to the theoretical exFAT
specification limits.
.It
Cluster sizes ranging from 512 bytes up to 32 MiB (kernel mounts are
constrained by the maximum buffer cache block size,
.Va vfs.maxbcachebuf ,
typically 64 KiB).
.It
Contiguous cluster allocation optimization bypassing FAT chain traversal
when the stream allocation possible flag is set.
.It
Full Unicode support with case-insensitive, case-preserving filename lookups
using the volume's on-disk Up-Case table.
.It
Lockless fast-path namecache lookup
.Pq Xr cache_fplookup 9
under VFS Safe Memory Reclamation (SMR).
.It
Directory entry sets that span across cluster boundaries.
.It
Dynamic allocation bitmap management and cluster heap synchronization.
.It
Clean unmount volume dirty state clearing and
.Va PercentInUse
boot sector statistics maintenance.
.It
Validation of 32-bit Boot Region Checksums on mount with automatic fallback
to the Backup Boot Region when the Main Boot Region is corrupted.
.It
Directory cluster reclamation and truncation on unlink.
.It
Enforcement of
.Va ActiveFat
constraints per exFAT specification section 3.1.13.1, rejecting volumes with
.Er EINVAL
if
.Va ActiveFat
is set on single-FAT file systems.
.It
Strict compliance with directory entry classification rules (sections 6.2
and 6.3), rejecting access on unrecognized critical entries and passing
through recognized benign entries (such as Volume GUID and TexFAT Padding).
.It
Valid Data Length
.Pq Va ValidDataLength
tracking and safe sparse gap zero-filling up to
.Va DataLength
prior to committing payload data.
.It
Automatic read-only mounting of Transactional exFAT
.Pq TexFAT
volumes formatted with two File Allocation Tables
.Pq Li NumberOfFATs = 2
to preserve filesystem consistency.
.It
Sparse stream querying via
.Xr lseek 2
.Pq Dv SEEK_DATA No and Dv SEEK_HOLE
and
.Xr ioctl 2
.Pq Dv FIOSEEKDATA No and Dv FIOSEEKHOLE
leveraging the stream
.Va ValidDataLength
boundary.
.It
NFS export and cold filehandle lookup
.Pq Xr fhtovp 9 .
.It
GEOM label detection
.Pq Pa /dev/exfat/<label> .
.El
.Sh MOUNT OPTIONS
The following options can be passed to
.Xr mount 8
or
.Xr mount_exfat 8 :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm ro
Mount the file system read-only.
.It Cm rw
Mount the file system read-write (default).
.It Cm sync
Perform all file system I/O operations synchronously.
.It Cm noatime
Do not update file access timestamps on reads.
.It Cm uid Ns = Ns Ar uid
Set the owner of all files in the file system to
.Ar uid .
The default is 0 (root).
.It Cm gid Ns = Ns Ar gid
Set the group owner of all files in the file system to
.Ar gid .
The default is 0 (wheel).
.It Cm mask Ns = Ns Ar mask
Specify the maximum file permissions mask.
The default is 0755.
.It Cm dirmask Ns = Ns Ar dirmask
Specify the maximum directory permissions mask.
The default is 0755.
.It Cm notrim
Do not issue TRIM commands when clusters are freed (default).
.It Cm trim
Issue
.Dv BIO_DELETE
(TRIM) commands to the underlying storage device when clusters are freed.
.El
.Sh IOCTLS
The following file-system-specific
.Xr ioctl 2
calls apply to files and directories on mounted
.Nm
file systems and are defined in the
.In fs/exfat/exfat_ioctl.h
header file:
.Bl -tag -width EXFATIOC_GETLABEL
.It Dv EXFATIOC_GETLABEL
.Pq Li "char[EXFAT_MAX_LABEL_LEN]"
Retrieve the volume label of the mounted file system.
The caller passes a character array of size
.Dv EXFAT_MAX_LABEL_LEN
(64 bytes).
Upon return, the buffer contains the NUL-terminated UTF-8 representation of the
on-disk volume label (up to 11 Unicode characters).
If the file system has no volume label, an empty string is returned.
.It Dv EXFATIOC_SETLABEL
.Pq Li "char[EXFAT_MAX_LABEL_LEN]"
Set or clear the volume label of the mounted file system.
The caller passes a NUL-terminated UTF-8 string of up to 11 Unicode
characters.
If an empty string
.Pq Qq ""
is passed, the existing volume label entry is deleted.
This operation requires administrative privilege
.Pq Dv PRIV_VFS_ADMIN
unless invoked by the file system mount owner, and fails with
.Er EROFS
if the file system is mounted read-only.
.El
.Pp
In addition, the following standard descriptor ioctl calls defined in
.In sys/filio.h
are supported on regular files:
.Bl -tag -width FIOSEEKDATA
.It Dv FIOSEEKDATA
.Pq Li "off_t"
Seek to the next data byte at or after the specified offset.
Offsets within valid data
.Pq below Va ValidDataLength
are unchanged; offsets at or beyond
.Va ValidDataLength
fail with
.Er ENXIO .
.It Dv FIOSEEKHOLE
.Pq Li "off_t"
Seek to the next hole byte at or after the specified offset.
If the offset lies within valid data, returns
.Va ValidDataLength ;
otherwise returns the offset unchanged.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount an exFAT partition located on
.Pa /dev/da0s1 :
.Pp
.Dl "mount -t exfat /dev/da0s1 /mnt"
.Pp
Mount an exFAT volume using its GEOM volume label:
.Pp
.Dl "mount -t exfat /dev/exfat/FLASHDRIVE /mnt"
.Pp
Mount an exFAT volume read-only with a custom owner and permission mask:
.Pp
.Dl "mount -t exfat -o ro,uid=1001,mask=0750 /dev/da0s1 /mnt"
.Pp
An entry in
.Pa /etc/fstab
can be configured as follows:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/dev/da0s1	/mnt/flash	exfat	rw,noatime	0	0
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr lseek 2 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr fsck_exfat 8 ,
.Xr glabel 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr mount_exfat 8 ,
.Xr newfs_exfat 8 ,
.Xr cache_fplookup 9
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
file system conforms to the official Microsoft exFAT File System
Specification.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 15.1 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
kernel driver and associated userland utilities were implemented for
.Fx .
